# **2. What Remains — Build Order ****&**** Effort**

## **2.1 Staff Development (Tab 6) — Highest priority**

This is the most complex remaining component. The data schema is already defined in the DB. Build order:

- 8a: Industry Digital Confidence — 8 statements per staff member, scored 1–5. Labels configurable via rag-schema.json.

- 8a: Digital Pedagogy Matrix — 15 dimensions per staff member, scored 1–5. Accessibility and GDPR flagged as value-critical.

- Gap analysis — auto-flags anyone below 2.5/5. Value-critical items always at top.

- Auto-generated action plan per staff member — surfaced from gap scores.

- 8b: Staff Development capturing — manual log per person, links to Interventions table.

- Aggregate Staff Confidence score — feeds area header and Overview Card.

*Estimated session effort: 2–3 focused sessions.*

## **2.2 College-wide Staff Development tab**

*Aggregates from all area.staffDevelopment records. Build after Tab 6 has data. Filter by campus, area, role, Digital Lead mode. Estimated: 1 session.*

## **2.3 Report Builder — 4 Word templates**

Client-side .docx generation using the docx library (already available in the build environment). Four templates:

- Head of Area — area-specific: RAG, AFI phases, dimension scores, interventions summary. 1–2 pages. Warm tone.

- Digital Lead — area-specific: indicator-level HC scores, action plans assigned to DL, CPD suggestions. 1 page.

- Neil Davies (weekly) — cross-college: activities this week, areas engaged, RAG movements, next week priorities. 1 page.

- Ben Manning (monthly) — strategic: baseline vs current RAG distribution, interventions delivered, impact narrative, forward look. 2–3 pages.

*Estimated: 2 sessions. The docx skill and Python toolchain are already in place in this build environment.*

# **3. Evidence Hub Integration**

The existing Evidence Hub (gwc25.github.io/Digital-Evidence-Hub) is a separate application. The Impact Hub is designed as its functional replacement, but integration should be managed carefully.

## **3.1 What each system currently does**

|  | **Evidence Hub (current)** | **Impact Hub (new)** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Primary purpose** | Evidence logging, quick capture, accountability tracking, VFM case studies, resource library | Area-by-area RAG assessment, health checks, staff development, LWB, individual activities, CPD, reporting |
| **Data model** | DB.entries (evidence log), threads, referrals, HoA tracker snapshots, resource library | DB.areas (35 areas with full data), DB.learningWithoutBarriers, DB.individualActivities, DB.myCPD |
| **Overlap** | Individual Activities, My CPD, LWB activities, Confetti / Next Actions | Same sections, same data model, compatible JSON schema |

## **3.2 Integration approach — three options**

Option A: Run both in parallel (recommended for now)

- Keep Evidence Hub live for quick capture, evidence logging, VFM, resource library.

- Use Impact Hub for area-level work: RAG, health checks, interventions, staff dev.

- Export dpc-data.json from Impact Hub monthly. Import selected data into Evidence Hub if needed.

- Timeline: parallel running through October 2026 governance review.

Option B: Merge into a single application

- Impact Hub absorbs Evidence Hub functionality. All data in one JSON file.

- Requires adding: Quick Capture, Evidence Log, VFM, Resource Library, Confetti/Next Actions to Impact Hub.

- Migration function already stubbed in data.js (migrateFromEvidenceHub).

- Realistic timeline: after Report Builder is done, probably January 2027.

Option C: SharePoint as the bridge

- Save dpc-data.json to a SharePoint document library (not OneDrive sharing — just a file in a library).

- No "Anyone with the link" sharing required. CE+/ISO compliant.

- Access via SharePoint URL changes to a direct .json link. Works with the existing fetch in data.js.

**Recommendation: Option A now, Option B at the January 2027 natural pause point.**

## **3.3 Data compatibility**

The Impact Hub schema is a strict superset of the Evidence Hub schema. All field names are identical where they overlap. The migration function in data.js (migrateFromEvidenceHub) maps old fields to new. No data will be lost in a merge. The 35 area codes are identical in both systems.

# **4. DevObs and Quality Team Integration**

## **4.1 Development Observations**

The schema is already designed to accept DevObs data. The integration points are:

- Health Checks Tab 7: assessmentMethod field already includes "observation" and "learning-walk" as values. A DevObs populates the same per-indicator scoring grid with the same 1–5 scale.

- Interventions Tab 3: type field already includes "learning-walk" and "observation". A Learning Walk record sits here with objectives, plan, reflection, attendees, and further action.

- Individual Activities: any observation-type activity can be logged here cross-college.

What needs building: a dedicated DevObs modal that pre-populates the Health Check scoring grid from a learning walk context, adds the lesson observation fields (lesson plan quality, learner engagement, questioning, feedback quality), and auto-creates an action point. This is a 1-session add-on to Tab 7.

Suggested field additions for a DevObs record (extend health check schema):

- lessonPlanProvided: boolean

- lessonAims: text

- learnerEngagement: 1–5

- questioningAndChallenge: 1–5

- feedbackQuality: 1–5

- overallLessonJudgement: text (not a grade — a narrative)

## **4.2 Quality team activities**

The following Quality cycle activities can be integrated into the Impact Hub:

| **Activity** | **Integration point** | **What to build** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Learning Walks | Tab 7 Health Checks + Tab 3 Interventions | DevObs modal (1 session) |
| Peer Reviews / COG | Tab 3 Interventions (type: peer-review) | Already works — just log as intervention |
| QIP Targets (digital) | AFI Phases per area | Already works — QIP target = AFI phase title |
| Teach Meets | Individual Activities (type: teach-meet) | Already works — log attendance and impact |
| PPRs / SARs (digital dimension) | Report Builder (Ben Manning template) | Build Report Builder — use monthly export as SAR data source |
| Learner Voice (digital) | HC assessmentMethod: learner-voice | Already works — log as HC record with learner voice method |
| Governance Reviews (Oct 26, Apr 27) | Report Builder (Ben Manning template) + RAG snapshots | Save Rating Snapshot before each governance review — history preserved |

