# **8. Technical Maintenance Notes**

## **8.1 Passwords**

Password is a SHA-256 hash stored in index.html. Never change the code — just regenerate the hash and push. Sessions already open will continue to work until the next page load. Old hash: replace the full 64-character string in index.html.

## **8.2 Adding a new area**

Open your dpc-data.json → add a new area object following the existing schema → save and import. The area code must be 2–3 letters. The hub renders whatever areas are in the JSON.

## **8.3 Schema updates**

If the Health Check indicators or RAG sub-criteria change, edit data/hc-schema.json or data/rag-schema.json and push to GitHub. The hub fetches these on every load. Existing scored records are unaffected — scores are stored by index, not by label.

## **8.4 Browser compatibility**

Tested on Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari (iOS). localStorage is used for all data persistence. Private/incognito mode loses data between sessions. Recommend using Chrome or Edge as primary browser for the hub.

## **8.5 WCAG 2.2 AA**

All components verified at WCAG 2.2 AA minimum. Key contrast ratios: --col-accent (#1d4e89) at 7.2:1 on white (AAA), --col-teal (#065f46) at 7.68:1 on white (AAA). If any colours are changed, verify contrast before pushing.

